From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] explorer: the taskbar's own look, whatever the windows' style

Every part of the look mixes and matches (David 2026-10-02: "Every aspect
has Classic, Rounded, Horizon, Glass as a choice"). The Rounded taskbar
came with the Rounded window style (Style\Rounded) and the Horizon and
Glass bars with Taskbar\Style; Settings now writes the taskbar's own look,
HKCU\Software\Stained Glass\Taskbar "Look" (0 Classic, 1 Rounded, 2
Horizon, 3 Glass), which rules when present: a Rounded bar with square
windows, a Classic bar with round ones. Without it, as before. Test:
test/taskbarlooks-gate.sh (mutant SG_MUTANT_BAR_FOLLOWS_WINDOWS).
---
--- a/programs/explorer/systray.c
+++ b/programs/explorer/systray.c
@@ -3215,6 +3215,21 @@
     if (sg_look > SG_LOOK_GLASS) sg_look = SG_LOOK_FLAT;
     /* the Rounded style's bar is the flat look's */
     sg_rounded = sg_reg_dword( L"Software\\Stained Glass\\Style", L"Rounded", 0 ) != 0 && sg_look == SG_LOOK_FLAT;
+    {
+        /* the taskbar's own look, whatever the windows' (Settings writes
+         * Taskbar\Look 0 Classic, 1 Rounded, 2 Horizon, 3 Glass; David
+         * 2026-10-02: every part mixes and matches) -- a Rounded bar with
+         * square windows, a Classic one with round windows */
+        DWORD look = sg_reg_dword( L"Software\\Stained Glass\\Taskbar", L"Look", ~0u );
+#ifdef SG_MUTANT_BAR_FOLLOWS_WINDOWS
+        look = ~0u;
+#endif
+        if (look <= 3)
+        {
+            sg_look = look == 2 ? SG_LOOK_HORIZON : look == 3 ? SG_LOOK_GLASS : SG_LOOK_FLAT;
+            sg_rounded = look == 1;
+        }
+    }
     if (sg_look == SG_LOOK_HORIZON) { sg_pal = &sg_horizon_palette; return; }
     if (sg_look == SG_LOOK_GLASS) { sg_pal = &sg_glass_palette; return; }
     switch (sg_reg_dword( L"Software\\Stained Glass\\Taskbar", L"Color", 0 ))
